   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "Note: Guide",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Breeze Voice Clone\n\nClone a voice from any audio clip and reuse it. The clip is the whole input - no text, no language setting.\n\n### How to use\n\n1. Sign in with your ComfyUI account. This is an API node, so it bills per use.\n2. Feed **audio**: a recording, an uploaded file through Load Audio, or - as wired in this graph - a line generated by Breeze Text to Speech, so nothing has to be uploaded to try it.\n3. `remove_background_noise = true` cleans room tone and hiss before cloning. Turn it off only for already-clean studio takes.\n4. Queue the prompt. The node returns `voice` (a reusable BREEZE_VOICE) and `preview` (the cloned voice speaking, saved here).\n5. The clone keeps the language of the source clip. There is no language input on this node and no need to declare one: it is detected from the sample. To move the same timbre into another language, pass the cloned `voice` into Breeze Voice Localize.\n\n### Sample quality\n\nTen to thirty seconds of clean, continuous speech gives the most stable clone. Very short clips (under 3 seconds) and clips with music under the voice clone poorly even with noise removal on.\n"
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## Breeze Voice Clone\n\nClone a voice from any audio clip and reuse it. The clip is the whole input - no text, no language setting.\n\n### How to use\n\n1. Sign in with your ComfyUI account. This is an API node, so it bills per use.\n2. Feed **audio**: a recording, an uploaded file through Load Audio, or - as wired in this graph - a line generated by Breeze Text to Speech, so nothing has to be uploaded to try it.\n3. `remove_background_noise = true` cleans room tone and hiss before cloning. Turn it off only for already-clean studio takes.\n4. Queue the prompt. The node returns `voice` (a reusable BREEZE_VOICE) and `preview` (the cloned voice speaking, saved here).\n5. The clone keeps the language of the source clip. There is no language input on this node and no need to declare one: it is detected from the sample. To move the same timbre into another language, pass the cloned `voice` into Breeze Voice Localize.\n\n### Sample quality\n\nTen to thirty seconds of clean, continuous speech gives the most stable clone. Very short clips (under 3 seconds) and clips with music under the voice clone poorly even with noise removal on.\n"
   }
  }
 ],
